# Packages devices/pro/check asserts are installed on pro, beyond what Ubuntu Server 26.04.1 puts
# there itself. This is not an image's input list the way devices/vip/packages is — pro was
# installed by hand from the ISO — so it is the other direction: the record of what was added, which
# `check` turns into a test. It cannot notice a package that should not be there; what should not run
# is in etc/pedal/masked-units instead.
#
# The kernel is deliberately absent: rtpi owns it (rtpi/devices/pro/device.env pins the release, and
# devices/common/check reads it back from the host), exactly as for vip.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the engine's own needs
# alsa-utils is what namchain's tools and every capture use (amixer, arecord, aplay, speaker-test).
alsa-utils
# scripts/sync-library mirrors the model and IR library with it.
rsync
# pedal-wifi speaks nl80211 in python; pedal-device's status reads the cost table with it.
python3
# chrt, taskset and flock (util-linux); ps (procps); modprobe (kmod).
util-linux
procps
kmod

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- building the engine here
# pro has a compiler and builds its own namchain (scripts/deploy-engine --host pro, flags in
# build.env), because it is x86 and the Mac cannot cross-build for it the way the image build does
# for vip.
build-essential
cmake
ninja-build
pkg-config
libasound2-dev
git

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- measuring it
# turbostat (SMI count, the real clock, package power and temperature) and perf. The versioned
# package follows the kernel, so the generic one is what is named: `turbostat` from
# linux-tools-common works through the kernel's own tools directory.
linux-tools-common
# mpstat and pidstat. Its three collection timers are masked: the tools are wanted, the cron-like
# accounting is not.
sysstat
# The thermal and power limits the first hour-long soak could not rule out (P4): RAPL constraints,
# throttle counters.
powercap-utils
# lvextend -r, for growing either volume into the 1.57 TB left unallocated.
lvm2
